# Mirrored shape of admin-ui/.env.development + .env.production.
# VITE_ vars are bake-time only (Vite injects them at npm run
# build / vite dev). Leaving VITE_APP_NAME blank keeps the SPA
# un-scoped — every app the caller's roles grant shows up in
# the sidebar. Setting it scopes the sidebar to one App: the
# SPA appends `?app=<value>` on GET /sso-admin/myMenu and the
# backend's MyMenuService.forCaller(auth, appName) returns only
# routes whose id_app points at that App.
#
# Value must match an `app.name` row in the DB exactly
# (case-sensitive; app.name is UNIQUE NOT NULL per App.java).
# The canonical `SSO-ADMIN` is seeded by
# postgres/init/09-seed-sso-admin-app.sh.
VITE_API_BASE=/api
# VITE_APP_NAME=SSO-ADMIN
